{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1405061-stats-of-the-great-beasts","id":1405061,"title":"Stats of the Great Beasts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-28T06:42:14-07:00","id":1405061,"title":"Stats of the Great Beasts?","content":"Where can I find the stats of Great Beasts summoned by Song of the Great Beast?<br /> <br /> AFAIK several very early books have some Great Beasts which can be summoned by it.<br /> <br /> Ways of the Wolf, a very cold book. The Beasts are the greatest of all, they are... spiritual creatures? All have Willpower 10, Rage 10, Gnosis 10, and can use them like Garou<br /> <br /> Another core book, I can\u2019t recall name, 1st ST Handbook? It has Ness, Underground Alligator, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T06:46:13-07:00","id":1405062,"title":"","content":"This Gift has many alternatives. Song of City Beast, Song of Great Dragon, etc. If it has Black Spiral Dancer version, I always think it will summon Nexus Crawler","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T07:12:41-07:00","id":1405065,"title":"","content":"Well if your going off a nexus crawler for the bsd version, remove the warp reality charm and replace it with something comparable to what matter of beast you are dealing with while retaining the stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T21:24:21-07:00","id":1405123,"title":"","content":"You named the only two major sources I remember for the Great Beasts. Mammoth is given a description of a Great Beast in Rage Across Appalachia.<br /> <br /> <b>Ways of the Wolf</b><ul><li>Yeti</li> <li>Sasquatch/Big Foot</li> <li>Willawau (a giant owl, I don't know what legend this comes from</li> <li>Dinosaurs</li> <li>Great Sharks</li> </ul>Incidentally, each of these are the kind of Great Beasts named in the gift description for first and second edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook (first edition)</b><ul><li>Lake Serpents (Loch Ness Monster, Champy, Ogopogo, etc.)</li> </ul>Sewer Gators are mentioned in the ST's Handbook, but it is not an example of a Great Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Rage Across Appalachia</b><ul><li>Mammoth</li> </ul><br /> The Great Beasts have physical stats. Each is different, because the stats are supposed to reflect the individual animal (or in the case of Yeti and such, the legendary beast). They typically have two very high physical attributes (usually Strength and Stamina), decent Perception, and low in everything else. They have high skills in the relevant Abilities an animal should have - Brawl, Survival, Primal Urge, Alertness, Athletics, Animal Ken, and the legendary beasts have Occult.<br /> <br /> They appear to have about 12 total health levels. In Ways of the Wolf, it is mentioned they have 10s in Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, and that they regenerate two wounds per round. If killed, the regenerate in the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, these should actually be easy for any ST to create. If you want other examples, I'd read Wikipedia or another source on Pleistocene Megafauna, and pick which ones may excite you. You could include terror birds, Irish Elk, wooly rhinoceroses, glyptotheriums, giant condors, or megatheriums. Another source would be a list of cryptids like giant squids, bunyips (!), mongolian death worms, yowies, giant spiders, and thunderbirds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T17:51:33-08:00","id":1421706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1405061-stats-of-the-great-beasts?p=1405123#post1405123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You named the only two major sources I remember for the Great Beasts. Mammoth is given a description of a Great Beast in Rage Across Appalachia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add one, Giant Kangaroo and Megalania in Rage Across Australia, Page 113 and 114","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-03-2020, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T17:16:20-08:00","id":1421878,"title":"","content":"Old sources for SotGB tend to run into a lot of early installment weirdness with their stats, to the effect of being rather underwhelming. Just make sure that they have physical stats that are impressive even by the standards of a fully pumped-up Crinos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T22:21:29-08:00","id":1421933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1405061-stats-of-the-great-beasts?p=1421878#post1421878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old sources for SotGB tend to run into a lot of early installment weirdness with their stats, to the effect of being rather underwhelming. Just make sure that they have physical stats that are impressive even by the standards of a fully pumped-up Crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. I think physical stats of planet-dinosaur in Book of World may be more appropriate, Nexus Crawler too, although you do need some edits<br /> <br /> These canon ones, especially Giant Kangaroo and Megalania, I can\u2019t see any \u201cvery impressive\u201d on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T07:43:33-08:00","id":1422032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1405061-stats-of-the-great-beasts?p=1421933#post1421933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree. I think physical stats of planet-dinosaur in Book of World may be more appropriate, Nexus Crawler too, although you do need some edits<br /> <br /> These canon ones, especially Giant Kangaroo and Megalania, I can\u2019t see any \u201cvery impressive\u201d on them</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the Bygone Bestiary will give you options to round out your bigger critters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}